0227b: test-backend-ops cases for the decode FA arm (0227). test_flash_attn_dec27: FLASH_ATTN_EXT in the dense 27B hybrid's layout (q a permuted view [256, T, 24] nb [4, 24576, 1024]; K q8_0 and V q4_0 permuted views [256, n_kv, 4] of a longer cache, nb [34, 1088, 272] and [18, 576, 144]), the mask as served (row t sees the keys up to its own token), 28 eval cases (two at the dispatch's crossover, 8,191 and 8,192 keys at 6 rows: with the switch at 1 the first must run on today's kernels and the second on the arm; the decisions check asks the gate the same, red first with GGML_TEST_FA_DEC27_DECISIONS=nomin; from the threshold on a run that tests the arm - the op cases, the red builds, a perf case below 8,192 keys - needs GGML_OPENCL_FA_DEC27=2, since at 1 those cases run today's kernels; 13,056 keys with a split that walks nothing, 8,960 cells with a hidden padded tail, 131,072 keys and the V-floor case - block maxima ~1e-6 under a row with no dominant key, which the kernel must pass (a P V phase without the normalised scale fails it) - among them): 4 to 8 rows at 1,013 and 4,096 keys, 4 / 6 / 8 rows at 32,768 and 77,297 keys, a hidden stretch, 16 query heads on 2, calls of 6 and 37 keys; one in the contiguous layout the gate refuses, and two of 12 and 16 rows whose row blocks the arm must not take. A case the arm does not serve runs on today's kernels at their bound, 5e-4. The fill: an amplitude a (kv head, key, block), and the last 8 keys carrying a good part of a row's weight at any depth, so a wrong scale, a dropped tail key and a lost block all move the answer. The bound against the CPU backend for a case on the arm, stated before any card run: 1e-5 below 16,384 keys, 2e-5 from there (the CPU's own distance from a double reference grows with depth; the lost-key reds sit more than 10 times above 2e-5). With GGML_OPENCL_FA_DEC27=1 a case fails when the backend's record shows no launch of the arm for it or a split count that is not the rule's ("[FA_DEC27] split=.."); without the switch the cases run on today's kernels and the arm must not have launched. Device-free: GGML_TEST_FA_DEC27_DECISIONS=1 (every case through the pure gate, the split for both cards; =red: every case in the contiguous layout must FAIL) and GGML_TEST_FA_DEC27_CPU=1 (every case on the CPU backend against a double-precision attention on ggml's dequantization: the CPU within half the bound, a dropped last key and a lost seam block a split each more than 10 times the bound; and what the card does with a 16-half block read of a mask run 2 bytes past a 4-byte boundary - the first build's read, the kernel's red build 7 - more than 10 times the bound in every case of an odd key count but one - the crossover's own case of 8,191 keys shows it at 7.9 times its bound and is named, not asked (11 cases ask the 10 times) - its figures the card's: 7.01e-4 against 7.02e-4 at 1,013 keys and 6 rows, 3.97e-2 at 77,297). Perf cases: 6 rows at 4,096, 32,768, 77,297 and 131,072 keys, 4 and 8 rows at 77,297.

